  "id": "COMPOUND:18998 - PROTEIN:685",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (+)-Secoisolariciresinol diglucoside and the Serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2A catalytic subunit beta isoform, mediated through the Gamma-secretase pathway. This relationship is supported by multiple independent pathways, all of which indicate that (+)-Secoisolariciresinol diglucoside acts as a target of several compounds, including 1-[3-methoxy-4-[(3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxyphenyl]ethanone, 4-Chloro-3,5-Dihydroxytoluene, and 5-N-Tricosylresorcinol. These compounds are all known to interact with Gamma-secretase, which in turn targets the Serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2A catalytic subunit beta isoform. The consistent presence of this interaction across different pathways suggests a plausible mechanism of action, where (+)-Secoisolariciresinol diglucoside may modulate the activity of Gamma-secretase, thereby influencing the expression or function of the phosphatase subunit. The evidence is robust and consistent, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
